What the Apache-2.0 license does NOT provide is:

  • Support — guaranteed response times, integration assistance,
    and maintenance commitments for your release cadence.
  • SLA / indemnification — contractual uptime and liability terms
    that enterprises typically require.
  • Priority features — SDK work prioritized for your roadmap.

Those are available under a paid support/services agreement. Pricing is
per-deal (one-time or per-device) and scoped to your integration.

